   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "OPERATION: OUT OF MEMORY · MiniMax H3 · 7 fixes in one graph\nBeyond the Frame\n\nRe-select your own model, encoder and VAE files in the loaders (left). Red nodes = a fix.\n\nFIX 01 · STOCK TEXT ENCODER (this workflow)\nThe 32B encoder alone needs ~15.7 GB. If you run out of memory before the first frame,\nuse OOM_H3_seven_fixes_ClipProj.json instead: 4B encoder + projection, ~5–8 GB, same wires.\nhttps://github.com/nicolab28/ComfyUI-ClipProj\n\nFIX 02 · PRUNED MODEL\nFull INT8 / BF16 were reported to flicker or render black. Pick a pruned file:\n  ~24 GB VRAM: pruned INT8 (ComfyUI default)\n  ~12 GB VRAM: pruned int8_convrot + --lowvram + lots of system RAM\n  https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/tree/main/diffusion_models\n\nFIX 07 · VRAM-Cleanup node\nInstall: ComfyUI Manager → 'Comfyui-Memory_Cleanup' (LAOGOU-666), or\ngit clone https://github.com/LAOGOU-666/Comfyui-Memory_Cleanup into custom_nodes.\nIt unloads every model after sampling so the VAE gets the whole card.\nTiled VAE Decode does NOT help with H3 (the H3 VAE already tiles inside).\nFrames must be n % 17 == 5: 5, 22, 39 … 124 (~5 s) … 209 (~8.7 s) … 243 (~10 s).\nOn 16 GB, crashes started above ~209 frames: render short clips, join them in the edit."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    1020,
    -760
   ],
   "size": [
    900,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 15,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "FIX 03 · THE ENGINE (outside the graph)\nSuddenly 4× slower after an update? One report: PyTorch 2.12.0+cu130 ≈ 16.8 s/step\nvs 2.14.1+cu130 ≈ 62.9 s/step, same workflow.\nRead the PyTorch / CUDA versions in the console at startup while everything is fast,\nwrite them down, and reinstall that version if an update slows you down.\n\nFIX 04 · THE WAREHOUSE (outside the graph)\nOut of memory with memory to spare? Add to the line that starts ComfyUI:\n  python main.py --disable-dynamic-vram\n--lowvram has no effect while Dynamic VRAM is on.\n\nFIX 05 · THE BAD LINE\nCrackling audio: update ComfyUI first. Then plain euler (this graph), no EasyCache\n(none in this graph), and a short clean audio draft as reference if it persists.\n\nFIX 06 · THE DISGUISE\nNo official fix for reference drift. Describe what matters precisely and repeat it\n(see the prompt: ONE watch, narrow black tie), keep clips short, watch the previews\nand stop early. Worth testing: run without --fast fp16_accumulation."
   ]
  }
 ],
